<!--
  Managed code stripping guard for IL2CPP builds (issue #8).

  HeroCat.Runtime saves GameState with Newtonsoft.Json, which finds property setters, constructors (including the
  GearPiece record's) and enum members by reflection. The linker cannot see those uses, so without this file a device
  build can silently drop them: saves then load back as defaults, or every launch starts a new profile. The editor
  never strips, so only a device build shows the bug.

  Whole assemblies are preserved on purpose. They are small, and state types added later (in any namespace, such as
  HeroCat.Sim.State, HeroCat.Sim.Rng.RngStream or HeroCat.Runtime.Save) are covered without editing this file.

  Newtonsoft.Json comes from com.unity.nuget.newtonsoft-json (Packages/manifest.json), Unity's fork that ships an
  AOT-safe build for IL2CPP (no System.Reflection.Emit). Preserving it whole avoids stripping of its own
  reflection-only paths (converters, contract resolvers).

  Unity reads link.xml only from Assets/, not from the local packages under src/, so this file lives here.
  GameRoot runs SaveSelfCheck at startup and logs an error if a round trip loses data.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="HeroCat.Sim" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="HeroCat.Runtime" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="Newtonsoft.Json" preserve="all" />
</linker>
